      "big_recognition": "Section 1374 gain 'taken into account' for an asset is limited to the gain actually recognized on that asset, so Class VI BIG is capped at the Class VI allocation ($400,000 drafted / $100,000 counter) even though the appraised Class VI BIG is $900,000.",
      "big_tax_offset": "The section 1374 tax passes through as a section 1366(f)(2) loss (library: irc_1374.md); modeled as offsetting ordinary income first. Pass-through mechanics themselves are outside the closed library (unverified general principle).",
      "equipment": "Class IV allocated $650,000 vs adjusted basis $240,000 -> entire $410,000 gain is section 1245 ordinary recapture (post-conversion depreciation of $410,000 >= gain). Stated equipment BIG $230,000 used for 1374.",
      "closing_costs": "$112,200 (3.2% of $3.1M) shown as memo-only; not included in tax computations (not a tax item in the library)."
    },
    "document_issue_flagged": "Buyer A's Exhibit A sums to $3,300,000 — $200,000 above the $3,100,000 price — and values vehicles at $210,000 and office furniture at $250,000 although the company register shows only $50,000 of vehicles and no furniture. 'As drafted' is modeled holding Exhibit A's Class IV ($650,000) and Class VI ($400,000), Classes III/V at register FMV, with Class VII as the residual ($1,610,000)."
  },
  "asset_sale_buyer_a_as_drafted": {
    "ordinary_income": 1020000,
    "capital_gain": 1610000,
    "entity_level_tax": 132300,
    "total_tax": 782749,
